{"step_index":71,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:48:43Z","input_tokens":1304,"cache_read_tokens":144067,"output_tokens":354,"content":"The background task confirmed that Node.js is **only available bundled with Adobe software** — not installed as a standalone development tool on this Windows machine. The project is designed to run on Termux/local dev, so you'll need to run the commands there.\n\nHere's exactly what to do on your dev machine (Termux or wherever Node.js is installed):\n\n```bash\n# 1. Pull the changes from GitHub (or copy the project folder)\ncd NagrikOne\n\n# 2. Install dependencies\nnpm install\n\n# 3. Make sure your .env file has DATABASE_URL and SESSION_SECRET set\n\n# 4. ⚠️ CRITICAL — Apply the new passwordHash column to your DB\nnpm run db:push\n\n# 5. Start dev server\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n> **Why `db:push` is mandatory**: The old code stored passwords only in Node.js memory (lost on restart). The fix adds a `passwordHash` column to your `User` table in PostgreSQL. Without running `db:push`, registration will throw a Prisma error.\n\n### If you want to install Node.js on this Windows machine too:\nDownload from **https://nodejs.org** (LTS version) → installer adds `node` and `npm` to your PATH automatically, then you can run everything from PowerShell here.","thinking":"The node search task completed. Node.js was found only in Adobe's bundled locations. The user needs to install Node.js properly to run the project. Let me continue with the current state and let the user know."}
